proofs.proof_tex:
The bound \(c_g\le f(a)\le C_g\) proved in \(\texttt{thm:causal-transfer}\), together with \(\texttt{ass:strict-slope}\) and \(\texttt{ass:variance}\), gives, for \(P\in\mathcal M\) and \(a\in J\),
\[
 \left(\frac{c_gc_\theta^2}{4V_\kappa}\right)^{1/3}
 \le
 \left\{\frac{f(a)\theta'(a)^2}{4\kappa(a)}\right\}^{1/3}
 \le
 \left(\frac{C_gC_\theta^2}{4v_\kappa}\right)^{1/3}. \tag{1}
\]
Integration over \(J\) and \(\texttt{def:spatial-clock}\) yield
\[
 |J|\left(\frac{c_gc_\theta^2}{4V_\kappa}\right)^{1/3}
 \le\mathcal V(P)\le
 |J|\left(\frac{C_gC_\theta^2}{4v_\kappa}\right)^{1/3}. \tag{2}
\]
Because \(J=[\delta,1-\delta]\) and \(0<\delta<1/2\), \(\lvert J\rvert=1-2\delta>0\). All other factors in the lower bound are positive. Uniformly in \(P\),
\[
 T_n(P)\ge n^{1/3}|J|
 \left(\frac{c_gc_\theta^2}{4V_\kappa}\right)^{1/3}
 \longrightarrow\infty. \tag{3}
\]

Assume now the two conditional premises in the theorem, and write
\[
 b_n=b_{\mathcal E}(T_n(P)),\qquad
 \widehat b_n=b_{\mathcal E}(\widehat T_n).
\]
The clock definitions give
\[
 \frac{\widehat T_n}{T_n(P)}
 =\frac{\widehat{\mathcal V}_n}{\mathcal V(P)}.
\]
The assumed uniform relative consistency, positivity, and continuity of the logarithm at one imply
\[
 \log\frac{\widehat T_n}{T_n(P)}=o_P(1) \tag{4}
\]
uniformly. Equation (3) and relative consistency also imply that \(T_n(P)\) and \(\widehat T_n\) diverge uniformly, the latter in probability. Since
\[
 \mathcal E'(v)=\beta+\frac{\gamma}{v}\longrightarrow\beta>0,
\]
the two inverse centerings eventually lie, with probability tending uniformly to one, in the stipulated interval of strict increase, and \(b_n,\widehat b_n\to\infty\).

On that event, the mean-value theorem supplies \(\widetilde b_n\) between \(b_n\) and \(\widehat b_n\) such that
\[
 \mathcal E'(\widetilde b_n)(\widehat b_n-b_n)
 =\log\frac{\widehat T_n}{T_n(P)}. \tag{5}
\]
Both endpoints diverge, so \(\widetilde b_n\to\infty\) uniformly in probability. From \(a_{\mathcal E}(T)=1/\mathcal E'(b_{\mathcal E}(T))\), (4)--(5) give
\[
 \frac{b_{\mathcal E}(\widehat T_n)-b_{\mathcal E}(T_n(P))}
 {a_{\mathcal E}(T_n(P))}
 =\frac{\mathcal E'(b_n)}{\mathcal E'(\widetilde b_n)}
 \log\frac{\widehat T_n}{T_n(P)}
 =o_P(1), \tag{6}
\]
because the derivative ratio tends to \(\beta/\beta=1\). Likewise,
\[
 \frac{a_{\mathcal E}(\widehat T_n)}{a_{\mathcal E}(T_n(P))}
 =\frac{\mathcal E'(b_n)}{\mathcal E'(\widehat b_n)}
 \longrightarrow1. \tag{7}
\]
The future-excursion premise supplies only the contemplated interpretation of these expressions as a center and scale. Equations (4)--(7) prove the plug-in equivalence conditional on clock consistency, not an excursion law or coverage.
